Modifications
-------------
HireMe continues from Dossier 1.14.0 (November 2026) and changes it as follows:

- The product, its identifiers, environment variables, database and Docker
  names, URL scheme, documentation and desktop app naming say HireMe instead
  of Dossier.
- Added a private cloud worker so background jobs, backups and inbox checks
  survive a request ending or a container sleeping.
- Added application packets: one folder or ZIP per application, served from
  private storage, plus a dated Google Drive history with optional per-snapshot
  link sharing.
- Added per-app MCP permissions and single-use owner reviews for email,
  deletion and external submission handoff.
- Added several application bots with a shared prompt template and a macOS
  helper that fills a bot's composer without ever sending.
- Added a Setup & health page and a bound on import expansion size.
- Removed the upstream usage ping's default destination. It now runs only when
  an operator configures HIREME_TELEMETRY_HOST.

HireMe is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the Dossier
project. Dossier is a separate project with its own maintainers and roadmap.

